Spec: Windows bounded connection planning

Purpose:
  Select one authenticated transport within the original application admission budget.

Owns:
  ./ConnectionPlanner.cs

Must:
  Expose the original absolute attempt deadline to trusted route acquisition without resetting budgets.
  Defer cancellation-source disposal until an in-progress raw-abort/cancel pass ends; reentrant release must still deliver cancellation and remain idempotent.
  Include authorization and preparation time before scheduling; direct-only spends the remaining total budget on direct.
  Permit relay only under the effective approved policy and never retry authentication, capability, capacity, cancellation or clock failures through another path.
  Bound active setup attempts independently by path, retaining a slot until late work actually terminates.
  Cancel raw transport handles before deferred disposal, dispose late successes and transfer exactly one result without replaying application bytes.
  Return selected path, fixed fallback reason and setup time separately from later business traffic.
  Reject unsupported prewarm and relay byte limits before transport IO.
